178 {"id": "C-R178-BADGE-SELECTOR", "severity": "medium", "actual": "3 red: LRS5 (library-row-strings-ui l.330) and PW1 / PW6 (purchased-collection-ui l.230 badgeText()). Both find the header badge with querySelector('span.border-accent'), a colour class that W2 removes. This is a test-selector break, not a rendering regression: in the real browser the badge renders at both viewports with the text 'Demo collection — no sign-in required', rgb(163,155,142) and border rgb(115,107,96). Both files are protected in section 2
